# screenshots taken while testing — kept on disk, not in the repo
*.png
# …except the app's own icons, which have to ship. This rule already ate them
# once: git add -A reported the folder as new, committed the two non-PNG files
# in it, and said nothing about the four it skipped. CI caught it.
!public/*.png

# The one-file predecessor. It stays on disk because it still opens with a
# double-click, but it is not ours to publish: its find/replace boxes ship
# pre-filled with the house numbers off a real company certificate, and this
# repository is public. Its successor is #/legacy in the app.
PDF-Editor.html

# Which real documents this machine has, and what is written inside them.
